Definitions

- "The Work" means the collection of files licensed under +THYME.
- "A Covered File" means any file that is part of the Work, whether or
  not the file itself carries a license notice.
- "A Modified File" means a Covered File whose contents you have changed
  or translated, or any other file that contains a substantial portion
  copied from a Covered File.
- "Your Own Files" means files that are neither Covered Files nor
  Modified Files, even when they are used together with, placed
  alongside, or take the place of Covered Files (for example content,
  configuration, data, and new templates, styles, or scripts written
  without copying a substantial portion of a Covered File).
- "A Larger Work" means a work that combines Covered Files or Modified
  Files with Your Own Files.
- "Built Output" means anything generated from Covered Files or Modified
  Files rather than written by hand, such as rendered pages and
  minified, bundled, or compiled assets.

Terms for Covered Files and Modified Files

- You are free to use, modify, and distribute the Work.
- Every Modified File stays under +THYME. You may not place a Covered
  File or a Modified File under different terms.
- If you distribute Covered Files or Modified Files, you must provide
  their complete source code, in the form best suited to editing them,
  together with a copy of this license.
- You must credit the original creator of the Work. This credit must
  appear with the source of the Covered Files and Modified Files, at
  minimum in a README file or equivalent documentation file. You must
  also keep any copyright and license notices already present in them.
- If your Modified Files change how the Work is built, installed,
  configured, or operated, including how it works with any external
  backends or frontends it depends on, you must document those changes
  clearly enough for someone else to build and operate your version.

Terms for Your Own Files

- Your Own Files are not covered by +THYME. You may license them under
  any terms you choose, whether open source or proprietary, and you are
  not required to provide their source code.

Terms for Larger Works

If you distribute a Larger Work, you may do so under any license,
provided that you:

- Keep the Covered Files and Modified Files within it under +THYME, and
  include a copy of this license.
- Credit the original creator of the Work in the Larger Work's
  documentation.
- Make it possible to tell which files are Covered Files or Modified
  Files, for example by keeping them in their own directory or by
  listing them.
- Do not impose terms that limit anyone's rights under +THYME in the
  Covered Files and Modified Files.

Terms for Built Output

- You may use, publish, and distribute Built Output under any terms you
  choose. +THYME makes no claim on what you publish with it.
- Built Output generated only from unchanged Covered Files carries no
